<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas FitzGerald, 10th Earl of Kildare</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1513">1513</a>–<a href="/years/1537">1537</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Silken Thomas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas FitzGerald, 10th <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/earl-of-kildare">Earl of Kildare</a>, known as Silken Thomas, led a rebellion against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> in 1534 after rumours that his father, the imprisoned lord deputy, had been executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. His forces besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> and killed Archbishop John Alen, but the rising was crushed in 1535. He was executed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyburn">Tyburn</a> with five of his uncles in 1537.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-fitzgerald-10th-earl-of-kildare.jpg" alt="Thomas FitzGerald, 10th Earl of Kildare" width="320" height="379" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Anthony van Dyck · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thomas_FitzGerald,_10th_Earl_of_Kildare.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
